  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nTest case:\n\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<input id=\"one\">\n<input id=\"two\">\n<input id=\"three\">\n<script>\n    one.addEventListener(\"blur\", () => three.focus());\n    one.focus();\n    two.focus();\n</script>\n```\n\nWebKit, Chrome, and Firefox all show the third input box focused when this test case is loaded. I may be misreading the [focus update steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#focus-update-steps), but it seems that they do not consider what happens when firing the `blur` focus event results in a nested call to the focusing steps. My reading of the specification is that no matter what happened in the event handler, the rest of the algorithm will finish focusing the original/outer *new focus target* and *new chain*.",
